# Analyser and developer tooling. Never installed by the image and never by the
# platform Test stage, so it is deliberately kept out of requirements.in: every
# package in the scanned set has to be defensible, and lint and SAST tooling
# does not run on the platform.
# Constrained to the runtime-and-test lock, so a package both sets need is
# pinned to ONE version. Without this the two locks resolved tomli
# differently (2.5.0 against 2.4.1) and could not be installed together,
# which is what CI must do to run lint, type check and tests (audit F-S00-08).
-c requirements.txt

ruff>=0.9
mypy>=1.14
types-PyYAML
bandit[toml]>=1.7
pip-audit>=2.7
pip-tools>=7.4
diff-cover>=9.0
anyio[trio]>=4.0

# python-docx: only docs/generate_guide.py imports it, so it is documentation
# tooling and does not belong in the image (audit F-283). hypothesis was
# removed outright: no test imports it.
python-docx>=1.1

# playwright: drives a real browser for scripts/smoke-browser.py. Dev-only and
# never installed by the image or the platform Test stage. Recorded reason: two
# defects reached production returning HTTP 200 with a broken page - a dead
# HTMX swap and a CSRF-less form - and no server-side assertion could see
# either. A console-error assertion sees both.
playwright
